1
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:08,230
Two straight rails are parallel.

2
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:10,520
A road crosses them at an angle.

3
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:14,800
It makes an angle of 58 degrees with the first rail.

4
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:17,950
What is the matching angle at the second rail?

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,550
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,100
The road crosses both rails in the same direction.

7
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:31,060
So the angle in the matching position at the second rail is also 58 degrees.

8
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:33,730
These are called corresponding angles.

9
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:37,710
Let's see all the angle facts for parallel lines.

10
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:42,840
Remember: when two lines cross, vertically opposite angles are equal.

11
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,250
And angles on a straight line add up to 180 degrees.

12
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:55,640
So if one angle is 58 degrees, the angle next to it is 180 minus 58, which is 122 degrees.

13
00:00:55,690 --> 00:00:59,830
A transversal crosses two parallel lines and makes 8 angles.

14
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:03,600
Angles in matching positions are corresponding angles.

15
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:04,640
They are equal.

16
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:06,590
Look for an F shape.

17
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:12,480
Alternate angles are between the parallel lines, on opposite sides of the transversal.

18
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:13,780
They are equal too.

19
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:15,630
Look for a Z shape.

20
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,890
Co-interior angles are between the lines, on the same side.

21
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:21,260
They are not equal.

22
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:23,210
They add up to 180 degrees.

23
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:25,130
Look for a C shape.

24
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:25,820
Your turn.

25
00:01:25,870 --> 00:01:27,540
What does a Z shape show?

26
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:30,790
Pause the video and choose.

27
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:32,950
A Z shape shows alternate angles.

28
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,480
They are equal.

29
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:36,560
The facts also work backwards.

30
00:01:36,610 --> 00:01:41,840
If corresponding or alternate angles are equal, then the lines are parallel.

31
00:01:41,890 --> 00:01:44,880
Always give a reason for each angle.

32
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:46,240
Here is the method.

33
00:01:46,290 --> 00:01:50,510
Step 1: mark the parallel lines and the transversal.

34
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,750
Step 2: start from a known angle.

35
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:57,650
Look for an F, Z or C shape that links it to the angle you want.

36
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:01,820
Step 3: corresponding and alternate angles are equal.

37
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:04,970
Co-interior angles add up to 180.

38
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:08,630
Step 4: write a reason next to every angle.

39
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:11,570
Parallel lines are cut by a transversal.

40
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:13,340
One angle is 58 degrees.

41
00:02:13,390 --> 00:02:15,870
Find its co-interior angle.

42
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:20,010
Co-interior angles add up to 180 degrees.

43
00:02:20,060 --> 00:02:23,380
180 minus 58 is 122 degrees.

44
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:28,090
Two alternate angles are 3 x plus 15, and 5 x minus 25.

45
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:29,240
Find x.

46
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:31,650
Alternate angles are equal.

47
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:34,780
So 3 x plus 15 equals 5 x minus 25.

48
00:02:34,830 --> 00:02:38,350
Subtract 3 x, and add 25: 40 equals 2 x.

49
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,240
So x equals 20.

50
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:46,480
Check: 3 times 20 plus 15 is 75, and 5 times 20 minus 25 is 75.

51
00:02:46,530 --> 00:02:49,700
Both angles are 75 degrees.

52
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:50,500
Your turn.

53
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:54,410
Alternate angles are 2 x plus 10, and 70 degrees.

54
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:54,970
Find x.

55
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:58,120
Pause and work it out.

56
00:02:58,170 --> 00:03:00,640
Alternate angles are equal.

57
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:02,680
2 x plus 10 equals 70.

58
00:03:02,730 --> 00:03:05,200
Subtract 10: 2 x equals 60.

59
00:03:05,250 --> 00:03:07,150
So x equals 30.

60
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:09,860
Two lines are cut by a transversal.

61
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:14,110
The corresponding angles are 72 degrees and 74 degrees.

62
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:16,440
Are the lines parallel?

63
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:20,570
For parallel lines, corresponding angles must be equal.

64
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:24,540
72 is not equal to 74, so the lines are not parallel.

65
00:03:24,590 --> 00:03:26,960
They will meet somewhere.

66
00:03:27,010 --> 00:03:32,540
Parallel lines have an angle of 110 degrees, and its co-interior partner, y.

67
00:03:32,590 --> 00:03:34,160
Here is Eli's working.

68
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:36,760
Which line goes wrong first?

69
00:03:36,810 --> 00:03:37,990
Line 1 is wrong.

70
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:41,140
Co-interior angles add up to 180 degrees.

71
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:45,530
Only corresponding and alternate angles are equal.

72
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:50,580
y equals 180 minus 110, which is 70 degrees.

73
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:54,580
Car parks often paint bays at an angle, not straight across.

74
00:03:54,630 --> 00:03:57,730
The lines of the bays are all parallel.

75
00:03:57,780 --> 00:04:03,830
If every bay meets the kerb at 60 degrees, the painters only need to set the angle once.

76
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:06,660
Corresponding angles do the rest.

77
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:07,980
One last question.

78
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:11,210
What is the co-interior angle to 95 degrees?

79
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:14,590
Pause the video and answer.

80
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:17,820
Co-interior angles add up to 180.

81
00:04:17,870 --> 00:04:21,020
180 minus 95 is 85 degrees.

82
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:25,570
To remember: corresponding angles, in an F shape, are equal.

83
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:28,900
Alternate angles, in a Z shape, are equal.

84
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:33,760
Co-interior angles, in a C shape, add up to 180 degrees.

85
00:04:33,810 --> 00:04:38,730
Equal corresponding or alternate angles prove that lines are parallel.

86
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:40,710
Always give reasons.

87
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:45,870
Great work! Now practise lesson 5.1 on Camday.
